    "caveat_not_split_source_vs_doc": "This count is SITES, not defects. It has NOT been split into code that computes with the literal versus documentation, docstrings, test fixtures and audits that quote it on purpose -- this audit's own file and muon_pin_three_values_probe are both in the char-13 group precisely because they DOCUMENT the stale value. The predecessor CODATA sweep made exactly this mistake and had to correct itself: its 'code that computes a wrong number' bullet was 'wrong for 87 % of its own count'. Do not quote 65 as a defect count. The split is the next step.",
